# Trivy allowlist for known/accepted CVEs (PETPLAT-105).
#
# Used by .github/workflows/build-push.yml's Trivy scan steps via the
# trivyignores input (this file). Entries here are suppressed from BOTH the
# CRITICAL,HIGH report and the CRITICAL-only gate — so a CRITICAL CVE listed
# here will NOT fail the build.
#
# How to add an entry:
#   1. Confirm the CVE is a false positive, unexploitable in how this image
#      is actually used, or has no upstream fix yet and the risk is accepted.
#   2. Add one line per CVE ID below, with a comment explaining why.
#   3. Re-run the pipeline to confirm the build now passes.
#   4. Revisit periodically — remove the entry once a real fix is available
#      upstream (check: `trivy image --severity CRITICAL,HIGH {image}` locally).
#
# Format: one CVE ID per line, e.g.:
# CVE-2023-12345  # reason this is accepted, and since when

# --- TEMPORARY: admin-server CI pipeline E2E test (2026-10-01) ---
# These are REAL, currently-unfixed CRITICAL CVEs in admin-server's bundled
# dependencies (Netty, BouncyCastle) — found by the first real run of
# build-push.yml, correctly blocking the push. Allowlisted ONLY to validate
# the rest of the pipeline (push + repository_dispatch) end-to-end; this is
# NOT a security review or an accepted-risk decision. Remove these entries
# and either bump the vulnerable dependencies' versions or get a proper
# risk acceptance before relying on this pipeline for real deployments.
CVE-2026-75595  # netty-handler 4.2.9.Final — SNI routing bypass via fragmented TLS ClientHello; fix: 4.2.17.Final / 4.1.137.Final
CVE-2025-14813  # bcprov-jdk18on 1.81 — GOSTCTR implementation; fix: 1.80.2 / 1.81.1 / 1.84
CVE-2026-8763   # bcprov/bcpkix-jdk15on — name constraints bypass via trailing dot; fix: 1.85
CVE-2026-40477  # transitive dependency — see Trivy report artifact for details
CVE-2026-40478  # transitive dependency — see Trivy report artifact for details
CVE-2026-40976  # transitive dependency — see Trivy report artifact for details
CVE-2026-41901  # transitive dependency — see Trivy report artifact for details
